answer:
Qualitative (categorical) predictors that have only two levels are incorporated by turning the factor into a single 0/1 indicator (dummy) variable.  
For each observation you set  

\[
x_i=\begin{cases}
1 & \text{if the person belongs to one level (e.g., female)}\\[4pt]
0 & \text{if the person belongs to the other level (e.g., male)}
\end{cases}
\]

and then include this dummy variable as a regular predictor in the linear regression model. In the Credit data example, the gender variable is coded this way, yielding a term \( \beta_1 \times \text{gender[Female]} \) in the model (p. 99).
